/*Q14. Write a Java program to form a string with the provided characters and display the resulting string.
Input Format:
• The first line contains an integer N, which represents the number of characters to be entered.
• The next N lines contain the characters.
Output Format:
• The output is the string formed by combining the entered characters.
*/
import java.util.Scanner;
 
public class FormString {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = Integer.parseInt(sc.nextLine().trim());
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            String line = sc.nextLine();
            sb.append(line.isEmpty() ? ' ' : line.charAt(0));
        }
        System.out.println(sb);
        sc.close();
    }
}
